for 74 minutes. The next year, the legendary Blackbird,

727
00:42:30,181 --> 00:42:34,180
the SR-71, entered service to begin more than 20 years of high

728
00:42:34,181 --> 00:42:40,180
altitude spy missions. In the early 1970s, supersonic

729
00:42:40,181 --> 00:42:44,180
F-15 Eagle set new standards for air-to-air combat and

730
00:42:44,181 --> 00:42:48,180
precision ground strikes. The Martin Marietta X-21

731
00:42:48,181 --> 00:42:52,460
Marietta X-24B lifting body, an experimental wingless craft

732
00:42:52,461 --> 00:42:56,280
introduced in 1973, validated the approach and landing

733
00:42:56,281 --> 00:42:59,620
techniques later employed by the space shuttle.

734
00:42:59,621 --> 00:43:03,940
And in 1977, the successful air launch of the Enterprise

735
00:43:03,941 --> 00:43:07,540
introduced the prototype craft for the space shuttle itself.

736
00:43:07,541 --> 00:43:11,460
We have mastered the supersonic regime very, very well.

737
00:43:11,461 --> 00:43:13,940
We have gone from merely penetrating it

738
00:43:13,941 --> 00:43:15,780
to actually thriving in it.

739
00:43:15,781 --> 00:43:16,980
The airplanes have changed.

740
00:43:16,981 --> 00:43:19,480
The facilities have changed greatly.

741
00:43:19,580 --> 00:43:21,880
About the only two things that haven't changed is that lake bed

742
00:43:21,980 --> 00:43:25,980
that's sitting out there and the people who fly the airplanes.

743
00:43:26,080 --> 00:43:30,320
We're pushing to go faster and farther and do more with what

744
00:43:30,420 --> 00:43:35,440
we've got, just like they were 60 years ago.

745
00:43:35,540 --> 00:43:38,340
Breaking the barrier many deemed unbreakable,

746
00:43:38,440 --> 00:43:41,940
the XS-1 proved the most significant event in aviation

747
00:43:42,040 --> 00:43:45,880
since the Wright brothers first took flight at Kitty Hawk.

748
00:43:45,881 --> 00:43:47,780
Take a look back on the history of flight

749
00:43:47,880 --> 00:43:49,960
over the last 100 years, we find that there

750
00:43:50,060 --> 00:43:51,780
were some great challenges.

751
00:43:51,880 --> 00:43:54,260
The greatest challenge of all was

752
00:43:54,360 --> 00:43:59,160
to master the transonic and supersonic environment.

753
00:43:59,260 --> 00:44:01,600
And that's what the X-1 gave to us.

754
00:44:01,700 --> 00:44:03,560
It opened up a new frontier.

755
00:44:03,660 --> 00:44:06,240
There was no limit to what we could do once we could get

756
00:44:06,340 --> 00:44:10,680
past that supposed barrier.

757
00:44:10,780 --> 00:44:15,880
And it turned out not to be such a big boogaboo after all.

758
00:44:15,881 --> 00:44:20,880
I was lucky to live through the thing, lucky to be involved.

759
00:44:20,980 --> 00:44:23,580
I was the right place, right time, at the right age,

760
00:44:23,680 --> 00:44:27,120
and had the capability of taking advantage of it.

761
00:44:27,220 --> 00:44:29,720
It's that simple.

762
00:44:29,820 --> 00:44:32,420
But if Jager's goal was simply defined,

763
00:44:32,520 --> 00:44:34,340
his mission was profound.

764
00:44:34,440 --> 00:44:37,840
Braced by the courage of pilots to face an unknown destiny,

765
00:44:37,940 --> 00:44:41,280
the triumphant flight of the XS-1 marked the end of an era

766
00:44:41,380 --> 00:44:45,880
in the history of aviation and the beginning of another.

767
00:44:45,881 --> 00:44:50,420
For more information on breaking the sound barrier, log on to chuckyeager.com.

